and plan out your  day if you're going to make a high value  purchase such as a tv electronics or  jewelry  make sure you do not store those in your  vehicle in view of other people  if possible consider leaving small  children at home so they don't get lost  in the crowds  if children are with you have a  predetermined location to meet in case  you are separated also make sure  children have your phone number so that  they can reach you if you do become  separated  only bring with you credit cards that  you actually intend to use  for that trip  many financial institutions allow credit  card holders to receive notifications  regarding account activity  we would suggest that you investigate  this option  so that if your credit card becomes  compromised your account can be frozen  and prevent further unauthorized  transactions  do not let other people see you enter  your pin number be careful as you're  entering your pin number and know who's  around you  if you're using cash do not carelessly  handle cash  and show others around you how much you  have  do not leave purses phones or other  small electronic devices in your vehicle  in plain view  criminals may be in parking lots looking  for people loading items into their  vehicles and then walking back into  stores to make additional purchases  it only takes a few seconds for a  criminal to break a window and remove  those items from your vehicle  have a backup shop with a friend or  family member if possible  when shopping at night park in well-lit  areas near the main entrances if  possible  and as always be aware of your  surroundings  in closing we wish all of our residents  and visitors a happy holiday season  please make sure or help us keep the  community safe this year by reporting  suspicious activity as always if you see  something say something  thank you with that i'll be happy to  answer any  um how questions have you been doing  this initiative this isn't the first  time this initiative has gotten to  